message: "If you use this software or its associated study, please cite it as below."
title: "Internal Representation Profiles for Detecting Compressive Shortcut Learning"
type: software
version: 2.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-26
authors:
  - family-names: Kociu
    given-names: Suela
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Turin, Italy"
    email: suelaresuli@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A reproducible synthetic benchmark and confirmatory protocol for evaluating
  whether task-structured separability, spectral concentration, and local
  sensitivity can identify shortcut-induced changes in neural-network hidden
  representations. The package distinguishes archived pilot findings from
  prospective confirmatory analyses and makes no claim of universal shortcut
  detection.
keywords:
  - shortcut learning
  - spurious correlations
  - neural representations
  - interpretability
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
